Subject: [PATCH] ksu: allow root to read and write app profiles, like its siblings

GET_APP_PROFILE and SET_APP_PROFILE are the only two commands in the whole
dispatch table gated on the manager alone. Every other command that touches
policy -- the allow and deny lists, whether a uid is granted root or has its
modules unmounted, the kernel features -- is reachable by root, and is_manager()
is a bare uid comparison anyway, so a root process can already act as the
manager by assuming its appid. The check therefore keeps nothing from root; it
only stops root-side tooling (like ksud) from reading or writing a profile
without impersonating the manager first.

This widens both to manager_or_root, the check its siblings already carry.

Each entry is anchored on its own .cmd/.name/.handler so the two hunks localise
uniquely and survive the table being reordered.
--- a/kernel/supercall/dispatch.c
+++ b/kernel/supercall/dispatch.c
@@ -866,10 +866,10 @@
     {
         .cmd = KSU_IOCTL_GET_APP_PROFILE,
         .name = "GET_APP_PROFILE",
         .handler = do_get_app_profile,
-        .perm_check = only_manager
+        .perm_check = manager_or_root
     },
     {
         .cmd = KSU_IOCTL_SET_APP_PROFILE,
         .name = "SET_APP_PROFILE",
         .handler = do_set_app_profile,
-        .perm_check = only_manager
+        .perm_check = manager_or_root
     },
